WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.035 --> 00:00:00.660
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:04.860
Kendall Square is simply
the densest collection

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:07.980
of life scientists in
the known universe.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.850
It's that culture of faculty
entrepreneurs, that's what

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:14.460
really drove Kendall Square.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:15.840
There was a lot of courage.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:20.850
People really were willing to
follow the science, take risks.

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.350
I thought one day,
people will be

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.500
able to work on cancer
at the molecular level.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.730
This was new technology
at a world historic level.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:34.620
Man had the ability to make
a biological organism that

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.870
may not have ever
appeared before

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.760
in the biological kingdom.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:41.850
This country, this
community, has not

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:45.300
decided that we should go
ahead with this research.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.870
You've got to see it in the
shadow of the atomic bomb.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:49.590
[BOOM]

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:53.190
They kept worrying that there
was an atomic bomb hidden away

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.200
in modern biology.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.640
The mayor of Cambridge
became quite alarmed.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:03.825
Visions of cloned
creatures infecting us.

00:01:03.825 --> 00:01:07.290
If worst comes to
worst, we could have

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:11.700
a major disaster on our hands!

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.420
It was a real wild west moment.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:15.560
It was really the
birth of an industry.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.880
30, 40 years ago,
scientists tended

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.950
not to think about the
commercial aspects of what

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:20.790
they were doing.

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:22.500
Today, everyone does.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.870
When I have an idea
for a new company,

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:28.140
I can go across the hall, and
I can say, has this been tried?

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:30.240
Do you know an
investor I can talk to?

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.145
Will you be on my board?

00:01:32.145 --> 00:01:34.320
All of medicine is
getting rethought

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.710
in terms of the fundamental
causes of disease.

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:42.050
Things that were death
sentences aren't any more.

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:47.000
That kind of revolution doesn't
occur very often in history.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:51.350
To have had the opportunity
to live through all of that

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.160
is a wonder.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:54.910
[MUSIC PLAYING]

